    {
      "id": "CSE-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-sobolev-multiplicity",
      "title": "Haar measure and rational multiplicity bound the cube integral",
      "statement": "The cube constant at y is at most exp(f)(1+4√n/t(y)²)^(2N)P∞/kg, with t(y)=min(1,least(y)) and N=n²f.",
      "hypotheses": "A positive cube side with 12n³s≤1 and 8n⁵s≤1, orthonormal bases at all real places, compatible gauge Haar measures, and a level-invariant automorphic continuous representative.",
      "correspondence": "Compare Lebesgue with Haar integration, thicken by finite level invariance, fold to the quotient and pack the bounded separated ratios of rational lifts.",
