    {
      "id": "CSE-03",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-sobolev-initial",
      "title": "Uniform evaluation to start the deep-cusp descent",
      "statement": "With P=8qN and β at order P+N, vector evaluation is at most (6β)^N D C(y)‖u‖² in squared norm. On the short neighborhood 1+4√n/t(y)²≤17√n/τ(x)².",
      "hypotheses": "The indefinite counting hypotheses, n≥8, g≥1, n^19≤b², compatible representatives of D isometries, and a deep point with 0<τ(x)<1/2. The neighborhood radius is at most log 2.",
      "correspondence": "The discrete-series bound provides β, summing the D scalar estimates gives D, and the neighborhood lower bound for the truncated least size supplies a common initial bound for the iteration.",
      "dependencies": [
        "CSE-01",
        "CSE-02",
        "DSD-02"
      ],
